Now chat.js: history slice may start with an AI turn (Anthropic/Gemini reject a conversation whose first message isn't `user`) and may contain consecutive same-role turns (image-only user messages are dropped by the new string filter). Fix: trim leading non-user turns and merge consecutive same-role turns.

In ask():
```js
const turn = (m) => ({ role: m.role, content: m.content });
const userTurn = { role: 'user', content: (text || '(без текста)') + attachBlock };
const hist = history.filter(m => m !== userMsg).map(turn);
```
Change to:
```js
const hist = mergeTurns(history.filter(m => m !== userMsg).map(turn));
```
And add:
```js
/* История режется по MAX_COPY, поэтому срез может начаться с хода ИИ или
 * содержать два одинаковых соседних хода (ход без текста отсекается выше).
 * Claude и Gemini такие последовательности отвергают (400) — приводим их к
 * виду user/assistant, начинающемуся с пользователя. */
function mergeTurns(list) {
  const out = [];
  for (const m of list) {
    const last = out[out.length - 1];
    if (last && last.role === m.role) last.content += '\n\n' + m.content;
    else out.push({ ...m });
  }
  while (out.length && out[0].role !== 'user') out.shift();
  return out;
}
```
This is testable if exported. The tests use source assertions for chat.js (no DOM). I could export `mergeTurns` for a behavioral test. chat.js imports store.js which uses idb — the test file imports chat.js source only via readFileSync, presumably because importing chat.js would fail (it references document only inside functions, so import is fine... but store.js at import time? Let me check store.js top-level for idb access). Risky. Existing tests do `codeOnly(fs.readFileSync(...))` for chat.js — so source assertions are the pattern. But a behavioral test is much better.

Let me check whether importing js/chat.js in node works: chat.js imports './store.js' and './ai.js' and './modelsui.js'. store.js top-level probably defines constants and functions only. modelsui.js too. If no top-level DOM access, import works. Let me test quickly with node -e import.

Let me try.

